min(), max(), and desc()
min() and max() give the smallest and largest values, and arrange(desc()) sorts from the largest to the smallest.

penguins |&gt;
  group_by(species) |&gt;
  summarize(
    lightest = min(body_mass, na.rm = TRUE),
    heaviest = max(body_mass, na.rm = TRUE)
  ) |&gt;
  arrange(desc(heaviest))

# A tibble: 3 × 3
  species   lightest heaviest
  &lt;fct&gt;        &lt;int&gt;    &lt;int&gt;
1 Gentoo        3950     6300
2 Chinstrap     2700     4800
3 Adelie        2850     4775

fct_relevel() and fct_collapse()
A factor’s first level is its reference level in a model. fct_relevel() moves a level to the front, and fct_collapse() combines several levels into one.

penguins |&gt;
  mutate(species = fct_relevel(species, "Gentoo")) |&gt;
  count(species)

# A tibble: 3 × 2
  species       n
  &lt;fct&gt;     &lt;int&gt;
1 Gentoo      124
2 Adelie      152
3 Chinstrap    68



penguins |&gt;
  mutate(island = fct_collapse(island, other = c("Dream", "Torgersen"))) |&gt;
  count(island)

# A tibble: 2 × 2
  island     n
  &lt;fct&gt;  &lt;int&gt;
1 Biscoe   168
2 other    176

A quick model
licorice_gargle comes from a randomised trial (Ruetzler et al., 2013) where patients gargled either licorice or sugar water before surgery and were asked about sore throat afterwards. We fit a logistic regression to compare the odds of a sore throat 30 minutes after surgery. An odds ratio below 1 means fewer sore throats with licorice.

licorice &lt;- licorice_gargle |&gt;
  mutate(
    gargle = factor(treat, levels = c(0, 1), labels = c("sugar", "licorice")),
    sore_throat = factor(pacu30min_throatPain &gt; 0, levels = c(FALSE, TRUE),
                         labels = c("no", "yes"))
  ) |&gt;
  drop_na(sore_throat)

logistic_reg() |&gt;
  fit(sore_throat ~ gargle, data = licorice) |&gt;
  tidy(exponentiate = TRUE, conf.int = TRUE)

# A tibble: 2 × 7
  term           estimate std.error statistic p.value conf.low conf.high
  &lt;chr&gt;             &lt;dbl&gt;     &lt;dbl&gt;     &lt;dbl&gt;   &lt;dbl&gt;    &lt;dbl&gt;     &lt;dbl&gt;
1 (Intercept)       0.568     0.193     -2.93 0.00337    0.386     0.824
2 garglelicorice    0.408     0.305     -2.93 0.00334    0.221     0.736

